{"name":"Baby Vegetable","hex":"#5d6942","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"vegetable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant.","A plant raised for some edible part of it, such as the leaves, roots, fruit or flowers, but excluding any plant considered to be a fruit, grain, herb, or spice in the culinary sense, and usually including non-plants lumped into the same culinary category, such as edible mushrooms and seaweed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to plants.","Of or relating to vegetables."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vegetable"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vegetable","blocks":[{"text":"Vegetables are edible parts of plants that are consumed by humans or other animals as food. This original meaning is still commonly used, and is applied to plants collectively to refer to all edible plant matter, including flowers, fruits, stems, leaves, roots, and seeds. An alternative definition is applied somewhat arbitrarily, often by culinary and cultural tradition; it may include savoury fruits such as tomatoes and squash, flowers such as broccoli, and seeds such as pulses, but exclude foods derived from some plants that are fruits, flowers, nuts, and cereal grains."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marketvegetables.jpg/330px-Marketvegetables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vegetable","wikidata":"Q11004"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marketvegetables.jpg/500px-Marketvegetables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marketvegetables.jpg/1280px-Marketvegetables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marketvegetables.jpg/500px-Marketvegetables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vegetables separated with baskets in a market in the Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarketvegetables.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/500px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/1280px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FruitArrangement.jpg/500px-FruitArrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An arrangement of fruits commonly thought of as culinary vegetables, including corn (maize), tomatoes, and various squash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFruitArrangement.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Filoma-Kohl_vor_der_Ernte.jpg/500px-Filoma-Kohl_vor_der_Ernte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Filoma-Kohl_vor_der_Ernte.jpg/500px-Filoma-Kohl_vor_der_Ernte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten